For any linear automorphism $\upphi\colon M\buildrel\sim\over{\setbox0=\hbox{$\longrightarrow$}\ht0=1.25pt\box0} M$, any $v,m\in M$, and $\epsilon=\pm 1$, we have
\begin{align}\label{TjAdEqn}
    \upphi\circ \mathrm{Ad}^{\epsilon}_{\Psi_t(z^v)} \circ \upphi^{-1}(z^m) = \mathrm{Ad}^{\epsilon}_{\Psi_t(z^{\upphi(v)})}(z^m)
\end{align}
in $\mr{\s{A}}_q^S$.  Here, $\Psi_t(z^v)$ is viewed as an element of $\Bbbk_{t,\upsigma}^{\Uplambda}\llb M\rrb$ for some cone $\upsigma$ containing $v$, and $\Psi_t(z^{\upphi(v)})$ is viewed as an element of $\Bbbk_{t,\upsigma'}^{\Uplambda}\llb M\rrb$ for some cone $\upsigma'$ containing $\upphi(v)$.  As usual, we define $\upphi$ on $\mr{\s{A}}_q^S$ via $\upphi(z^m)\coloneqq z^{\upphi(m)}$, and similarly for $\upphi^{-1}$.

\begin{align}\label{TjAdEqn}
    \upphi\circ \mathrm{Ad}^{\epsilon}_{\Psi_t(z^v)} \circ \upphi^{-1}(z^m) = \mathrm{Ad}^{\epsilon}_{\Psi_t(z^{\upphi(v)})}(z^m)
\end{align}

Note that $\upphi$ induces a $\Bbbk_t$-algebra isomorphism $\upphi\colon\Bbbk_t^{\Uplambda}[M]\otimes_{\Bbbk_t[z^v]} \Bbbk_t\llb z^v\rrb\rar \Bbbk_t^{\Uplambda}[M]\otimes_{\Bbbk_t[z^v]} \Bbbk_t\llb z^{\upphi(v)}\rrb$, so the left-hand side of \eqref{TjAdEqn} becomes \begin{align*}
    \upphi(\Psi_t(z^v)^{\epsilon} \upphi^{-1}(z^m) \Psi_t(z^v)^{-\epsilon}) = \Psi_t(z^{\upphi(v)})^{\epsilon} (z^m) \Psi_t(z^{\upphi(v)})^{-\epsilon}.
\end{align*}
